  "body": "### What is the issue with the Fetch Standard?\r\n\r\n1. These are not should requirements. They are musts.\r\n2. They return non-Infra values.\r\n3. The usage of headings and question marks seems to lead to some bugs, such as not being able to navigate to the caller of [https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#should-response-to-request-be-blocked-due-to-mime-type?](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#should-response-to-request-be-blocked-due-to-mime-type?)\r\n\r\nIdeally we'd change Fetch, CSP, and Mixed Content around the same time so we can have this continue to be somewhat consistent.\r\n\r\nMaybe something like:\r\n\r\n> To determine if a response _response_ to a request _request_ **is blocked due to its MIME type**:\r\n> 1. ...\r\n> 2. Return true.\r\n\r\n@antosart @carlosjoan91 thoughts?",
